To refresh: re-run the download in packages/srl/test/w3c (see git history of this dir).

This pin is on gh-pages, not on an open pull request: #1175 (the SPARQL-RL
rename, which the previous pin tracked) has merged, and gh-pages has since moved
past it. The spec is still in development, so a refresh can still change the
language under us — as this one did.

What this refresh changed, relative to the #1175 head we pinned before:

  Removed syntax. The changelog entry of 2026-08-12 records "FOR ?var IN
  <shape>" removed, three weeks after 2026-07-18 added it under GH-1074. The
  grammar file did not follow until w3c/data-shapes#1191 pointed out that
  ForClause and the IF rule production were still in the BNF and still used by
  test files; commits 58fdfc6 ("Remove 'FOR' from SRL grammar and tests") and
  cfbcd3c ("Remove rule IF syntax") took both out on 2026-08-24. There is now
  one rule production — RULE iri? HeadTemplate 'WHERE' 'DATA'? BodyPattern —
  and no FOR, IF or THEN anywhere in the grammar.

  So syntax/ lost the five tests that covered them (syntax-ruleset-structure-07
  .. -11) and rewrote -06 from the IF form to the RULE form: 144 entries down to
  139. Both baselines drop those five names; nothing else in either moves. Our
  parser dropped the same two constructs in step, which is why -06 still passes.

  Renamed prefix. Every manifest now labels the test vocabulary `srlt:` rather
  than `srt:`. The namespace IRI is unchanged, so the api harness — which
  resolves the Turtle and matches on the IRI — never saw it. The srl harness
  matches the prefixed names textually and did: its regex moved with the label.
  A future refresh that changes the label again has to move it again.

